{"url": "https://www.dal.ca/faculty/gradstudies/programs/graduate-programs.html", "final_url": "https://www.dal.ca/faculty/gradstudies/programs/graduate-programs.html", "status": 200, "method": "http", "fetched": "2026-10-24", "text": "Graduate programs | Faculty of Graduate Studies | Dalhousie University\nSkip to main content\nClose\nFaculty of Graduate Studies\nDal.ca Home\nmyDal\nDal Online\nBrightspace\nFaculty of Graduate Studies\nDal.ca Home\nLogin\nmyDal\nDal Online\nBrightspace\nOpen Dal\nWhy Dal?\nWhy Dal?\nAt Dal, you\u2019ll get an education that empowers you and join a community dedicated to your success. All that, and you\u2019ll never be more than 30 minutes from a beach.\nWhy Dal? Overview\nAbout Halifax and Nova Scotia\nInnovative programs and research\nThe Killam advantage\nMeet our community\nMeet our graduate students\nMeet our faculty\nAbout FGS\nMeet our team\nResources for faculty and staff\nPrograms\nPrograms\nDalhousie graduate programs empower you to make a difference. Study with leading faculty members in over 90 master's and 45 PhD programs.\nPrograms Overview\nGraduate programs\nJoint doctoral program\nProfessional master's degree programs\nApply for graduate studies\nApply for graduate studies\nLearn how to apply to a graduate studies program at Dalhousie University, and the application requirements for Canadian and international students.\nApply for graduate studies Overview\nHow graduate studies works\nAdmission requirements\nInternational students\nEnglish language requirements\nHow to apply\nSubmit supporting documents\nFind your supervisor\nAfter you apply\nYou've been accepted. What's next?\nVisiting graduate research students\nApply for a standalone course\nVisiting student graduate studies\nFinance your studies\nFinance your studies\nDalhousie offers a competitive rate of tuition and generous funding to ensure our students are focused on their studies not their wallets.\nFinance your studies Overview\nTuition and fees\nHow to finance your studies\nSupport for diverse students\nScholarships and bursaries\nMaster's scholarships, bursaries and awards\nDoctoral scholarships, bursaries and awards\nInternational student scholarships, bursaries and awards\nScholarships and bursaries\nCurrent students\nCurrent students\nSee how we support the success of current graduate students, including a list of resources available on our internal myDal site.\nCurrent students Overview\nProfessional development\nDal GradPD\nOur partners\nOnline professional development options\n3 Minute Thesis\nFormer finalists share their secrets to 3 Minute Thesis success\nThe OpenThink Initiative\nBIPOC Mentorship Network\nMicroResearch\nGrad student life\nGrad Orientation Station\nMeet the mentors\nGet involved\nFamily life\nPostdoctoral researchers\nPostdoctoral researchers\nAs a Dalhousie Postdoctoral researcher, you will refine your professional skills, enrich your research and transition to being a scholar in your own right.\nPostdoctoral researchers Overview\nFellowship funding\nDonald Hill Family Postdoctoral Fellowships\nKillam Postdoctoral Fellowships\nCanada Postdoctoral Research Award (CPRA)\nDal.ca Home\nFaculty of Graduate Studies\nPrograms\nGraduate programs\nGraduate programs\nExplore your path\nChoose from 100+ graduate programs at Dalhousie \u2014 including thesis-based degrees, professional (course-based) master\u2019s programs, and PhD programs. Whether you\u2019re a current undergrad exploring next steps or a working professional building toward your goals, you\u2019ll find flexible options designed to help you advance.\nBrowse all graduate programs\nProfessional (Course-Based) Master's Programs\nFlexible, career-focused programs you can complete in as little as 12 months. These programs offer hands-on, course-based learning with no thesis required \u2014 ideal for developing new skills, advancing your career, or transitioning into a new field.\nExplore Professional Master's Programs\nProfessional Degrees (Entry-to-Practice)\nIf you\u2019ve completed previous university study or already hold an undergraduate degree, you can explore Dalhousie\u2019s professional, entry-to-practice programs. These programs prepare you for regulated professions\u2014such as law, medicine, and dentistry\u2014by combining academic learning with extensive hands-on training.\nLaw (JD): A first-class legal education that opens pathways to diverse careers.\nMedicine (MD): Hands-on, interprofessional experience starting in your first year.\nDoctor of Dental Surgery (DDS): Learn and practice in state-of-the-art clinic and lab facilities.\nDental Hygiene (BDH / BDH (Hons)): Gain practical experience with patients using the latest equipment and technology.\nJoint Doctoral Program (JDP)\nStudy and conduct research across both Dalhousie and a partner institution through a jointly supervised PhD program. You\u2019ll complete requirements at both universities, spend time at each, and graduate with a single jointly awarded PhD supported by parchments from both institutions.\nLearn more about JDP\nAdmissions & Contact\nSome programs have additional requirements beyond the Faculty of Graduate Studies minimums. If you\u2019re unsure what\u2019s needed, contact the department directly via the program links below.\nNot quite ready to speak with a program advisor?\nOur team is here to help. Email us at graduate.studies@dal.ca with any general questions about graduate study at Dal.\nAgriculture\nArchitecture\nBiochemistry & Molecular Biology\nBiological Engineering\nBiology\nBiomedical Engineering\nBusiness (Master of Science)\nBusiness Administration (MBA \u2011 Corporate Residency)\nBusiness Administration (MBA \u2011 Financial Services)\nBusiness Administration (MBA \u2011 Leadership)\nChemical Engineering\nChemistry\nCivil and Resource Engineering\nCivil Engineering and Planning*\nClassics\nClinical Vision Science\nCommunication Sciences and Disorders\nCommunity Health & Epidemiology\nComputational Biology and Bioinformatics\nComputer Science\nComputer Science (Applied)\nDigital Innovation\nEarth and Environmental Sciences\nEconomics\nElectrical and Computer Engineering\nElectronic Commerce\nEngineering\nEngineering Mathematics\nEnglish\nEnvironmental Engineering\nEnvironmental Studies\nFood Science and Technology\nFrench\nGerman\nHealth\nHealth Administration\nHealth Informatics\nHealth Promotion\nHistory\nIndustrial Engineering\nInformation (Formerly Library and Information Studies)\nInformation Management\nInterdisciplinary PhD\nInternational Development Studies\nInternetworking\nJournalism\nKinesiology\nLaw\nLeisure Studies\nMarine Management\nMaster of Science \u2011 Occupational Science\nMaterials Engineering\nMathematics\nMechanical Engineering\nMedical Neuroscience\nMedical Physics\nMedical Research\nMicrobiology & Immunology\nMineral Resource Engineering\nMusicology\nNursing\nOccupational Therapy Entry Level\nOceanography\nOral and Maxillofacial Surgery\nPathology\nPeriodontics\nPharmaceutical Science\nPharmacology\nPhilosophy\nPhysics and Atmospheric Science\nPhysiology & Biophysics\nPhysiotherapy\nPlanning\nPolitical Science\nProsthodontics*\nPsychiatry\nPsychology & Neuroscience\nPublic Administration\nPublic Administration (Management)\nResource & Environmental Management\nSocial Anthropology\nSocial Work\nSociology\nStatistics\nReady to apply?\nStart your application through the Graduate Application Portal. Click below to get started.\nApply to a graduate program now\nDALHOUSIE UNIVERSITY\nFaculty of Graduate Studies\nHenry Hicks Academic Administration Building, Room 314\nPO Box 15000 | Halifax, NS B3H 4R2 Canada\n902.494.2485\nContact FGS\nCurrent Students\nFaculty & Staff\ndalgradstudies\nDalGradStudies\ndal.gradstudies\nDalhousieFGS\nhttps://ca.linkedin.com/showcase/dalhousie-university-faculty-of-graduate-studies/\nDal.ca Home\nFaculty of Graduate Studies\nPrograms\nGraduate programs\nBack to Top\nCampus Directory\nPrivacy Statement\nTerms of Us